# Vite only loads .env.development in dev mode and .env.production in
# build/production mode (`vite build`, which is what `pnpm build` /
# `wrangler deploy` actually run) -- it does NOT read wrangler.jsonc's
# `vars` block for import.meta.env (that's a separate, server-runtime-only
# mechanism). Without this file, the production client bundle had NO
# value at all for these -- not "accidentally pointed at localhost", but
# literally `undefined` -- which silently no-op'd the WebSocket hook
# (useRealtimeInbox bails out immediately when the URL is falsy, so no
# realtime AND no fallback polling ever ran in production) and made every
# direct browser->engine call in wa-api.ts (templates, media, account)
# resolve against a broken relative "undefined/..." URL.
#
# TEMPLATE — copied to .env.production (gitignored) by `pnpm install`.
# Edit .env.production, not this file.
#
# Keep this in sync with apps/web/wrangler.jsonc's `vars.VITE_ENGINE_URL`
# and apps/worker's deployed name -- both must point at the SAME publicly
# reachable engine worker URL. No secrets belong in this file -- it ships in the client
# bundle for anyone to read.
VITE_ENGINE_URL=https://YOUR-ENGINE-WORKER.YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev
VITE_WA_API_URL=https://YOUR-ENGINE-WORKER.YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev

# Optional: Sentry DSN for browser error reporting (leave empty to disable).
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
